{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1465168-rite-of-the-opened-caern-limit","id":1465168,"title":"Rite of the Opened Caern Limit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-24T11:15:23-07:00","id":1465168,"title":"Rite of the Opened Caern Limit","content":"It is said that if the player win the duel against the spirit of the Cairn he gain as many dices/points/levels in the corresponding attribute, ability or power for the rage gnosis and willpower. But there's no indication of how many time it can be performed, how long it last or if it's permanent.<br /> I cant believe it can be permanent because it would be well too powerfull, especially for a level 1 rite. We can discuss with the ST to decide the right solution but i'm curious to know how other players play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T11:53:11-07:00","id":1465171,"title":"","content":"You can find this in the second edition Players Guides on page 104. A less detailed version appears in the revised Players Guide to Garou on page 101. They seem to be found right before the book talks about caern types and the kind of powers they have.<ul><li>Customarily, each success equals one bonus die to be distributed among the characters (participating in the rite) as the ritemaster sees fit. If the bonus could go to more than one dice pool, the affected pool must be chosen when the bonus is awarded.</li> <li>Typically, these bonus dice have an effective duration of one day and may not be saved up.</li> <li>A player may benefit from a specific power only once during a single day, so if the player is awarded more bonus dice in the same area, he loses any bonus he may already have had.</li> <li>A caern can be utilized a number of times during a single day equal to its rank level. Thus, a Rank 4 caern can be accessed only four times before it is drained and in need of a recharging. There is no special procedure for recharging a caern; simply leaving it alone for an interval is all that is required.</li> <li>During times of desperate circumstance, a caern can be called upon for more endowment, but only at great risk. If the ritemaster attempts to draw additional bonus dice from a caern that has already been drained, the difficulty rises by 1.</li> <li>Typically the Master of the Rite (or another sept officer) determines who can open the caern and typically performs the rite himself.</li> </ul>This information really should be incorporated into the main corebook.<br /> <br /> I had the same questions and posted on this forum a year ago, and nobody knew the answer. It was by pure luck I ran across this section in an old book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T12:20:33-07:00","id":1465173,"title":"","content":"It is in W20. The Rite explicitly links to page 301, where the caern types and appropriate bonuses are listed. But the write-up is lacking. The roll is an extended, contested roll. Since it is over, once you reach the level of the caern, the bonuses are equal to the caern level, plus successes in excess, I guess.<br /> <br /> No info on how long the bonuses last. My guess would be, as long as appropriate. If an attack is imminent, the bonuses should last till the attack is over, if the character is trying to get the bonuses for an epic quest, the bonuses might last longer. But, having the caern opened for too long, might have some negative consequences, so it shouldn't be permanent. But that's all my take on the flavour of the game, since there aren't any rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}